@startuml
!include ../../../../../../plantuml/sodexo-theme.puml

title View and manage the approval queue — End-to-end interaction
header Sat, 25 Jul 2026 · End-to-end discovery sequence
footer (c) Developed by <b>Mohit Kanwar</b>

hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 90

actor "Approver" as Actor
participant "Approval Workspace" as Surface
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Accommodation Experience API" as Edge
participant "Booking Workflow Service" as Service1
database "Service-owned data" as Data
queue "Kafka event platform" as Events



group 1. List actionable requests within the approver’s organisational scope.
  Actor -> Surface: List actionable requests within the approver’s organisational scope
  Surface -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/approvals?status=pending
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service1: List actionable requests within the approver’s organisational scope.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service1 -> Service1: Authorise and query
  Service1 -> Data: Read or commit Booking Workflow Service data
  Service1 --> Edge: Scoped result
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service1 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

group 2. Return request, offer, policy, conversation, and authority evidence.
  Actor -> Surface: Return request, offer, policy, conversation, and authority evidence
  Surface -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/approvals/{approvalId}/context
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service1: Return request, offer, policy, conversation, and authority evidence.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service1 -> Service1: Authorise and query
  Service1 -> Data: Read or commit Booking Workflow Service data
  Service1 --> Edge: Scoped result
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service1 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

@enduml
